@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam classBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
hide empty members
title COLORS — Class Diagram\nConceptual module and domain model of the procedural implementation
class "Browser controller\njs/code.js" as Browser <<module>> {
  userId : Number
  firstName : String
  lastName : String
  + doLogin()
  + saveCookie()
  + readCookie()
  + doLogout()
  + addColor()
  + searchColor()
}
class "Login.php" as Login <<endpoint>> {
  + getRequestInfo()
  + sendResultInfoAsJson(obj)
  + returnWithError(err)
  + returnWithInfo(firstName, lastName, id)
}
class "AddColor.php" as Add <<endpoint>> {
  + getRequestInfo()
  + sendResultInfoAsJson(obj)
  + returnWithError(err)
}
class "SearchColors.php" as Search <<endpoint>> {
  + getRequestInfo()
  + sendResultInfoAsJson(obj)
  + returnWithError(err)
  + returnWithInfo(searchResults)
}
class "database.php" as DB <<module>> {
  + connectDatabase() : mysqli
}
class User <<entity>> {
  ID : int {PK, auto increment}
  FirstName : varchar(50)
  LastName : varchar(50)
  Login : varchar(50)
  Password : varchar(50)
}
class Color <<entity>> {
  ID : int {PK, auto increment}
  Name : varchar(50)
  UserID : int
}
Browser ..> Login : POST login, password
Browser ..> Add : POST color, userId
Browser ..> Search : POST search, userId
Login ..> DB : connects
Add ..> DB : connects
Search ..> DB : connects
Login ..> User : SELECT from Users
Add ..> Color : INSERT into Colors
Search ..> Color : SELECT from Colors
User "1" -- "0..*" Color : owns (intended relationship)
note bottom of DB
  Reads private configuration outside
  the web root; returns a MySQLi connection.
end note
note bottom of User
  User and Color map to Users and Colors tables.
  Multiplicity expresses intended ownership.
  The schema declares no foreign key, and
  the API does not validate user ownership.
end note
legend bottom
<<module>> and <<endpoint>> group existing functions; these are not PHP/JS classes.
<<entity>> models stored records, not implemented ORM classes.
Dependencies show calls or data access; there is no inheritance hierarchy.
endlegend
@enduml
